          "message": "fix(vectors/kani): raise open_from_bytes_never_panics unwind bound to 89 (sq-kycq5) [SONNET-4.6] (#1553)\n\nThe #[kani::unwind(40)] bound on `open_from_bytes_never_panics` was less\nthan MAX_LEN = HEADER_LEN + 32 = 88, and its inline comment \"// > MAX_LEN\"\nwas factually wrong. The setup loop runs up to MAX_LEN = 88 iterations;\nall other loops in the cone (AlignedBytes aligned copy, fingerprint scan,\nindex-validation) are also bounded by MAX_LEN. The minimum sufficient\nbound is MAX_LEN + 1 = 89, matching the sq-gnvfc pattern for the sibling\n`open_validated_v2_tail_never_panics` harness. The wrong bound would have\nfired an unwinding assertion (incomplete proof) in the nightly Kani lane.\n\nThe _DOMAIN_ADMITS_A_WELL_FORMED_STORE compile-time self-check already\ncovers this harness's MAX_LEN domain — no duplication needed.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-05T08:49:08Z",
          "tree_id": "88e625e224ba38b7be1e3eb97456a125df547ed8",
